The browser adaptation was developed in PGMaps and is mirrored as editable
TypeScript and React source in web/src. It adds local browser execution, input
validation, normalized hectare accounting, bounded workloads, structured
predicates, event histories, partial-cut and salvage accounting, seeded fixed-plan
yield sensitivity, Float64 raster exports, maps and browser reports. Corrections
and extensions are documented in the pinned PGMaps host's
docs/forestry-castor.md and docs/forestry-castor-source-audit.md.

This is an adapted implementation, not an official BC Government product or an
assertion of complete numerical equivalence with an R/SpaDES simulation. It does
not reproduce absent gamma calibration, the external Java cellular automaton,
provincial PostgreSQL preparation or the companion disturbance/road/fire/caribou
modules. The original R module remains separately preserved in this repository.

web/source.json records the exact PGMaps host revision and hashes of all mirrored
source files. The host's public/data/forestry-castor directory carries the unchanged
dataCastor example, its provenance, full licence and data notice; that sample is
included at build time instead of duplicated in this source overlay.
